{"success":true,"code":null,"message":null,"requestId":"T3ccbe61e8165406db9c4de491d2a0573","data":{"contentData":{"id":"RAW_04ce0133","displayDocument":"<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">DeepSeek released <strong><a href=\"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSpec/blob/main/DSpark_paper.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">DSpark</a></strong>, a speculative decoding framework, with open-source checkpoints and training code. It is a serving optimization, not a new model. The checkpoints <code>DeepSeek-V4-Pro-DSpark</code> and <code>DeepSeek-V4-Flash-DSpark</code> reuse the existing V4 weights, with a draft module attached.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The DeepSeek research team also <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-DSpark\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">open-sourced DeepSpec</a>, an MIT-licensed codebase for training and evaluating speculative decoding drafters. The work targets one problem: faster large-model inference in busy production serving.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-tl-dr\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>TL;DR</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>DSpark pairs a parallel draft backbone with a tiny sequential head to cut suffix decay.</li>\n   <li>A confidence head and load-aware scheduler verify more tokens when GPUs are idle, fewer when busy.</li>\n   <li>Offline, accepted length rises 26–31% over Eagle3 and 16–18% over DFlash.</li>\n   <li>In production on DeepSeek-V4, per-user generation runs 60–85% faster than the MTP-1 baseline.</li>\n   <li>Output stays lossless, and the checkpoints plus DeepSpec training code are open-source.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <h2 id=\"h-what-is-dspark\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What is DSpark?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Speculative decoding splits generation into two roles. A small draft model proposes a block of tokens. The full target model then verifies that block in one forward pass.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Rejection sampling accepts the longest valid prefix and appends one bonus token. Because the rule preserves the target distribution exactly, there is no quality loss. DSpark keeps this guarantee. It changes how tokens are drafted and how many get verified.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-the-latency-math-it-optimizes\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Latency Math it Optimizes</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Per-token latency follows one equation from the paper: <code>L = (T<sub>draft</sub> + T<sub>verify</sub>) / τ</code>. Here <code>τ</code> is the number of tokens accepted per cycle. Speedup comes from three levers only.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can draft faster, lowering <code>T<sub>draft</sub></code>. You can draft better, raising <code>τ</code>. Or you can verify smarter, reducing wasted <code>T<sub>verify</sub></code>. DSpark pulls all three levers at once.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-it-works-semi-autoregressive-generation\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How It Works: Semi-Autoregressive Generation</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Earlier drafters force a trade-off. Autoregressive drafters like Eagle3 condition each token on prior ones. That gives strong acceptance, but drafting cost grows with block size.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Parallel drafters like DFlash produce the whole block in one pass. Drafting stays cheap, but each position ignores its neighbors. The result is ‘multi-modal collision’ and rapid acceptance decay along the suffix.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">DSpark splits drafting into two stages. A heavy parallel backbone, DFlash in their setup, produces base logits for every position. Then a lightweight sequential head adds a prefix-dependent bias before sampling each token.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The default sequential head is a Markov head. It only looks at the immediately preceding token. A low-rank factorization (rank 256) keeps it cheap, even with large vocabularies.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once position one samples ‘of’, the head boosts ‘course’ and suppresses ‘problem’. An optional RNN head tracks the full block prefix. It adds only marginal gains, so the Markov head ships as the default.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The payoff shows up position by position. DSpark inherits the parallel backbone’s high first-token accuracy. The sequential head then holds acceptance steady deep into the block.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Training freezes the target model and reuses its embedding and output head. A total-variation loss is the key term. Minimizing that distance directly maximizes the draft’s acceptance rate.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-it-works-confidence-scheduled-verification\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How It Works: Confidence-Scheduled Verification</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">More draft tokens do not always mean more speed. Verifying tokens that will be rejected wastes batch capacity under heavy load. DSpark adds two parts to fix this.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A confidence head outputs a score for each draft position. The score estimates the chance that token survives verification, given accepted predecessors. It is supervised by the analytical per-step acceptance rate.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Raw neural confidence is usually overconfident. So the research team applies Sequential Temperature Scaling, a post-hoc calibration step. It cuts expected calibration error from 3–8% down to about 1%.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A hardware-aware prefix scheduler then sets the verification length per request. It uses a profiled throughput curve, <code>SPS(B)</code>, measured once at startup. When GPUs are idle, it verifies more tokens. When GPUs are busy, it verifies fewer.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The scheduler uses an early-stopping rule to stay lossless. The appendix section gives a counterexample showing why a naive global search would leak information.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-metrics\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Metrics</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Offline tests cover math, code, and daily chat. Targets include Qwen3-4B, 8B, 14B, and Gemma4-12B. DSpark beats both baselines on accepted length across every domain.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Against Eagle3, macro-average accepted length rises 30.9%, 26.7%, and 30.0% on the three Qwen3 sizes. Against DFlash, gains are 16.3%, 18.4%, and 18.3%. A 2-layer DSpark even beats a 5-layer DFlash.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The sequential head adds little cost. Scaling draft length from 4 to 16 adds only 0.2–1.3% per-round latency. In return, accepted length improves by up to 30%.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Production results come from DeepSeek-V4-Flash and V4-Pro under live traffic. The baseline is MTP-1, the prior single-token setup. At matched throughput, per-user speed rises 60–85% on Flash and 57–78% on Pro. The shipped configuration is DSpark-5, a five-token draft block with the Markov head.</p>\n  <figure class=\"wp-block-table\">\n   <table class=\"has-fixed-layout\">\n    <thead>\n     <tr>\n      <th>Drafter</th>\n      <th>Drafting style</th>\n      <th>Block cost</th>\n      <th>Suffix acceptance</th>\n      <th>Verification length</th>\n     </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Eagle3</td>\n      <td>Autoregressive</td>\n      <td>Grows with block size</td>\n      <td>High, stable</td>\n      <td>Fixed</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>DFlash</td>\n      <td>Parallel</td>\n      <td>Near-constant</td>\n      <td>Decays fast</td>\n      <td>Fixed (full block)</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>MTP-1</td>\n      <td>Single-token (MTP)</td>\n      <td>Low</td>\n      <td>—</td>\n      <td>Static 2 tokens</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>DSpark</td>\n      <td>Parallel + sequential head</td>\n      <td>Near-constant</td>\n      <td>High, stable</td>\n      <td>Dynamic, load-aware</td>\n     </tr>\n    </tbody>\n   </table>\n  </figure>\n  <h2 id=\"h-use-cases-with-examples\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Use Cases With Examples</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Structured workloads gain the most from longer verification. In code generation, acceptance is naturally high. The scheduler can verify long prefixes with little waste, so coding agents stream output faster.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Open-ended chat behaves differently. A confidence-threshold sweep raised chat acceptance from 45.7% to 95.7%. The confidence head flags uncertain suffix tokens so they can be pruned.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Math reasoning sits between the two. Its acceptance rose from 76.9% to 92.5% in the same sweep. Long step-by-step traces benefit from steady deep-block acceptance.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">High-concurrency serving is the headline case. At moderate load, the scheduler runs roughly 4–6 verified tokens per request. As concurrency rises, it trims that budget to protect throughput.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-try-it\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Try It</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">DeepSpec runs in three stages: data preparation, training, then evaluation. A config selects the algorithm and target model. Evaluation benchmarks a trained draft checkpoint across nine datasets.</p>\n  <div class=\"dm-code-snippet dark dm-normal-version default no-background-mobile\" snippet-height=\"\" style=\"background-color:#abb8c3\">\n   <div class=\"control-language\">\n    <div class=\"dm-buttons\">\n     <div class=\"dm-buttons-left\"></div>\n     <div class=\"dm-buttons-right\">\n      <a id=\"dm-copy-raw-code\"><span class=\"dm-copy-text\">Copy Code</span></a>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <pre class=\" no-line-numbers\"><code id=\"dm-code-raw\" class=\" no-wrap language-php\"># Install dependencies\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# Train a DSpark draft against a Qwen3-4B target.\n# The algorithm and target are chosen by the config, e.g.\n# config/dspark/dspark_qwen3_4b.py\nbash scripts/train/train.sh\n\n# Evaluate the trained draft across the 9 benchmark datasets.\n# Set in the eval config:\n#   target_name_or_path = Qwen/Qwen3-4B\n#   draft_name_or_path  = ~/checkpoints/deepspec/dspark_block8_qwen3_4b/step_latest\nbash scripts/eval/eval.sh</code></pre>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The default configs assume one node with 8 GPUs. Reduce <code>CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</code> for fewer. Note the target cache can be large, near 38 TB for the Qwen3-4B setting.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For the production checkpoints, the draft module attaches to the existing V4 weights. The Hugging Face cards include a minimal inference example in the <code>inference</code> folder. No retraining of the target model is required.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The interactive demo below shows the mechanism. Pick a drafter, a domain, and a GPU-load level. Watch the draft block, the confidence scores, and the scheduler’s verification budget change in real time. The numbers are illustrative, modeled on the paper’s reported behavior.</p>\n  <!-- DSpark Decoding Simulator — paste into a WordPress \"Custom HTML\" block only -->\n  <div style=\"max-width:960px;margin:0 auto;\">\n   <iframe class=\"lazyload\" id=\"dspark-sim-frame\" title=\"DSpark Decoding Simulator\" loading=\"lazy\" srcdoc=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n&lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;\n&lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;\n&lt;title&gt;DSpark Decoding Simulator&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n  :root{\n    --bg:#ffffff; --panel:#f6f8fc; --panel2:#eef2fb; --ink:#16203a;\n    --muted:#5b6680; --line:#dfe5f2; --blue:#4d6bfe; --blue-soft:#e7ecff;\n    --green:#1f9d57; --green-soft:#e3f7ec; --red:#e0413b; --red-soft:#fdeceb;\n    --amber:#e8920c; --amber-soft:#fdf1dd; --radius:14px;\n  }\n  *{box-sizing:border-box}\n  #dspark-sim{\n    font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\n    color:var(--ink); background:var(--bg); padding:22px; max-width:920px; margin:0 auto;\n    line-height:1.5;\n  }\n  #dspark-sim .sim-head{margin-bottom:6px}\n  #dspark-sim h1{font-size:22px; margin:0 0 4px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:-.2px}\n  #dspark-sim .sub{color:var(--muted); font-size:14px; margin:0 0 18px}\n  #dspark-sim .controls{\n    display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:14px;\n    background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius);\n    padding:16px; margin-bottom:16px;\n  }\n  #dspark-sim .ctl label{display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--muted);\n    text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.5px; margin-bottom:8px}\n  #dspark-sim .seg{display:flex; gap:6px; flex-wrap:wrap}\n  #dspark-sim .seg button{\n    flex:1; min-width:64px; padding:9px 6px; border:1px solid var(--line); background:#fff;\n    color:var(--muted); border-radius:9px; font-size:13px; font-weight:600; cursor:pointer;\n    transition:all .15s;\n  }\n  #dspark-sim .seg button:hover{border-color:var(--blue)}\n  #dspark-sim .seg button.on{background:var(--blue); color:#fff; border-color:var(--blue)}\n  #dspark-sim .slider-row{display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px}\n  #dspark-sim input[type=range]{flex:1; accent-color:var(--blue); height:4px}\n  #dspark-sim .val{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; font-weight:700; font-size:14px;\n    min-width:48px; text-align:right; color:var(--ink)}\n  #dspark-sim .stage{\n    background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius);\n    padding:18px 16px; margin-bottom:16px;\n  }\n  #dspark-sim .stage-title{font-size:13px; font-weight:700; margin:0 0 4px}\n  #dspark-sim .stage-note{font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 14px}\n  #dspark-sim .track{display:flex; gap:7px; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:flex-end}\n  #dspark-sim .tok{\n    width:60px; border-radius:11px; border:1px solid var(--line); background:#fff;\n    text-align:center; padding:8px 4px 7px; position:relative; transition:all .2s;\n  }\n  #dspark-sim .tok .lab{font-weight:700; font-size:15px; font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace}\n  #dspark-sim .tok .role{font-size:9px; color:var(--muted); text-transform:uppercase;\n    letter-spacing:.4px; margin-bottom:2px; height:11px}\n  #dspark-sim .tok .cbar-wrap{height:5px; background:var(--line); border-radius:3px; margin-top:6px; overflow:hidden}\n  #dspark-sim .tok .cbar{height:100%; background:var(--blue); border-radius:3px}\n  #dspark-sim .tok .cnum{font-size:10px; color:var(--muted); margin-top:3px; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  #dspark-sim .tok.anchor{background:var(--blue-soft); border-color:var(--blue)}\n  #dspark-sim .tok.accepted{background:var(--green-soft); border-color:var(--green)}\n  #dspark-sim .tok.rejected{background:var(--red-soft); border-color:var(--red)}\n  #dspark-sim .tok.dropped{opacity:.4; background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#fff,#fff 5px,#f0f0f4 5px,#f0f0f4 10px)}\n  #dspark-sim .tok.bonus{background:var(--green-soft); border-color:var(--green); border-style:dashed}\n  #dspark-sim .badge{position:absolute; top:-8px; right:-6px; width:18px; height:18px;\n    border-radius:50%; font-size:11px; line-height:18px; color:#fff; font-weight:700}\n  #dspark-sim .badge.ok{background:var(--green)} #dspark-sim .badge.no{background:var(--red)}\n  #dspark-sim .cut{display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; margin:14px 0 4px;\n    font-size:12px; color:var(--amber); font-weight:600}\n  #dspark-sim .cut .line{flex:1; height:1px; background:var(--amber); opacity:.4}\n  #dspark-sim .stats{display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:12px; margin-bottom:16px}\n  #dspark-sim .stat{background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius);\n    padding:14px 12px; text-align:center}\n  #dspark-sim .stat .num{font-size:26px; font-weight:800; color:var(--blue); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\n    letter-spacing:-.5px}\n  #dspark-sim .stat .cap{font-size:11px; color:var(--muted); margin-top:3px; font-weight:600}\n  #dspark-sim .cmp{background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:16px}\n  #dspark-sim .cmp-title{font-size:13px; font-weight:700; margin:0 0 12px}\n  #dspark-sim .bar-row{display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; margin-bottom:9px}\n  #dspark-sim .bar-name{width:64px; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--muted)}\n  #dspark-sim .bar-track{flex:1; background:var(--panel2); border-radius:6px; height:22px; overflow:hidden}\n  #dspark-sim .bar-fill{height:100%; border-radius:6px; display:flex; align-items:center;\n    justify-content:flex-end; padding-right:7px; color:#fff; font-size:11px; font-weight:700;\n    transition:width .4s; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  #dspark-sim .bar-fill.e3{background:#9aa6c2} #dspark-sim .bar-fill.df{background:#6f8bf6}\n  #dspark-sim .bar-fill.ds{background:var(--blue)}\n  #dspark-sim .legend{display:flex; gap:16px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:12px; font-size:11px; color:var(--muted)}\n  #dspark-sim .legend span{display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:5px}\n  #dspark-sim .dot{width:11px; height:11px; border-radius:3px; display:inline-block}\n  #dspark-sim .ftr{margin-top:18px; padding-top:14px; border-top:1px solid var(--line);\n    display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px}\n  #dspark-sim .ftr a{color:var(--blue); text-decoration:none; font-weight:600}\n  #dspark-sim .ftr b{color:var(--ink)}\n  @media (max-width:640px){\n    #dspark-sim{padding:14px}\n    #dspark-sim .controls{grid-template-columns:1fr}\n    #dspark-sim .stats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}\n    #dspark-sim .tok{width:48px}\n  }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;dspark-sim&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;sim-head&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;DSpark Decoding Simulator&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;See how the draft block, confidence scores, and the load-aware scheduler set accepted length. Numbers are illustrative, modeled on the paper's reported behavior.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;controls&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ctl&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;label&gt;Drafter&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;seg&quot; id=&quot;seg-draft&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;button data-v=&quot;eagle3&quot;&gt;Eagle3&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button data-v=&quot;dflash&quot;&gt;DFlash&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button data-v=&quot;dspark&quot; class=&quot;on&quot;&gt;DSpark&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ctl&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;label&gt;Domain&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;seg&quot; id=&quot;seg-domain&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;button data-v=&quot;math&quot; class=&quot;on&quot;&gt;Math&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button data-v=&quot;code&quot;&gt;Code&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button data-v=&quot;chat&quot;&gt;Chat&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ctl&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;label&gt;Draft block size &amp;gamma;&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;slider-row&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;sl-gamma&quot; min=&quot;4&quot; max=&quot;16&quot; step=&quot;1&quot; value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;span class=&quot;val&quot; id=&quot;v-gamma&quot;&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;ctl&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;label&gt;GPU load (concurrency)&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;slider-row&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;sl-load&quot; min=&quot;0&quot; max=&quot;100&quot; step=&quot;1&quot; value=&quot;35&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;span class=&quot;val&quot; id=&quot;v-load&quot;&gt;35%&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;stage&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;stage-title&quot;&gt;Draft block &amp;rarr; schedule &amp;rarr; verify&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;stage-note&quot; id=&quot;stage-note&quot;&gt;DSpark drafts the whole block in parallel, then the hardware-aware scheduler keeps a confident prefix before the target verifies it.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;track&quot; id=&quot;track&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cut&quot; id=&quot;cut&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;scheduler cut&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;line&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cut-txt&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;stats&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stat&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;num&quot; id=&quot;s-tau&quot;&gt;0&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cap&quot;&gt;Accepted length &amp;tau;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stat&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;num&quot; id=&quot;s-budget&quot;&gt;0&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cap&quot;&gt;Verify budget&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stat&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;num&quot; id=&quot;s-speed&quot;&gt;0&amp;times;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cap&quot;&gt;Speedup vs 1-token&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stat&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;num&quot; id=&quot;s-waste&quot;&gt;0&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cap&quot;&gt;Tokens saved/step&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cmp&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;cmp-title&quot;&gt;Accepted length by drafter &amp;mdash; Qwen3-4B, current domain (Table 1)&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;bar-row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-name&quot;&gt;Eagle3&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-fill e3&quot; id=&quot;b-e3&quot;&gt;0&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;bar-row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-name&quot;&gt;DFlash&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-fill df&quot; id=&quot;b-df&quot;&gt;0&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;bar-row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-name&quot;&gt;DSpark&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-fill ds&quot; id=&quot;b-ds&quot;&gt;0&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;legend&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class=&quot;dot&quot; style=&quot;background:var(--blue)&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;anchor&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class=&quot;dot&quot; style=&quot;background:var(--green)&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;accepted&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class=&quot;dot&quot; style=&quot;background:var(--red)&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;rejected&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class=&quot;dot&quot; style=&quot;background:#c9cfde&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;dropped by scheduler&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ftr&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;span&gt;Illustrative simulator &amp;mdash; faithful to trends in the DSpark paper, not exact engine output.&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;span&gt;Built by &lt;b&gt;Marktechpost&lt;/b&gt; &amp;middot; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSpec&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;DeepSpec&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function(){\n  var state={draft:&quot;dspark&quot;, domain:&quot;math&quot;, gamma:8, load:35};\n\n  // Illustrative per-position conditional acceptance, modeled on Figure 2 (Qwen3-4B).\n  function cond(draft, domain, k){ // k is 1-indexed position in the block\n    var t=k-1, c;\n    var P={\n      math:{eagle3:[0.81,0.05,3,1], dflash:[0.82,0.06,4,-1], dspark:[0.88,0.05,6,-1]},\n      code:{eagle3:[0.77,0.03,3,1], dflash:[0.78,0.10,3,-1], dspark:[0.85,0.04,5,-1]},\n      chat:{eagle3:[0.53,0.21,2.5,1], dflash:[0.62,0.10,3,-1], dspark:[0.72,0.05,3,1]}\n    };\n    var p=P[domain][draft], base=p[0], amp=p[1], tau=p[2], dir=p[3];\n    if(dir&gt;0){ c=base+amp*(1-Math.exp(-t/tau)); }      // rising/stable\n    else { c=base+amp*Math.exp(-t/tau); }              // decaying\n    return Math.max(0.30, Math.min(0.985, c));\n  }\n\n  // Table 1 accepted lengths (Qwen3-4B) used for the comparison bars.\n  var TABLE={\n    math:{eagle3:4.62, dflash:4.85, dspark:5.70}, // MATH500 column\n    code:{eagle3:4.16, dflash:4.74, dspark:5.38}, // HumanEval column\n    chat:{eagle3:2.39, dflash:3.07, dspark:3.64}  // MT-Bench column\n  };\n\n  // Illustrative steps-per-second capacity curve. Higher load -&gt; steeper falloff.\n  function sps(batchTokens, load){\n    var k=0.05+0.95*Math.pow(load/100,1.4);   // load steepens the decay\n    return 1/(1+k*batchTokens);\n  }\n\n  var TOKENS=[&quot;E&quot;,&quot;F&quot;,&quot;G&quot;,&quot;H&quot;,&quot;I&quot;,&quot;J&quot;,&quot;K&quot;,&quot;L&quot;,&quot;M&quot;,&quot;N&quot;,&quot;O&quot;,&quot;P&quot;,&quot;Q&quot;,&quot;R&quot;,&quot;S&quot;,&quot;T&quot;];\n\n  function schedule(surv, load){\n    // Greedy admission along the prefix while expected throughput keeps rising.\n    var tau=1, B=2, best=tau*sps(B,load), budget=0;\n    for(var j=0;j&lt;surv.length;j++){\n      var nt=tau+surv[j], nB=B+1, th=nt*sps(nB,load);\n      if(th&gt;best){ best=th; tau=nt; B=nB; budget=j+1; } else { break; }\n    }\n    return budget;\n  }\n\n  function render(){\n    var g=state.gamma, draft=state.draft, domain=state.domain, load=state.load;\n\n    // conditional acceptance + cumulative survival for each draft position\n    var cond_=[], surv=[], acc=1;\n    for(var k=1;k&lt;=g;k++){ var c=cond(draft,domain,k); cond_.push(c); acc*=c; surv.push(acc); }\n\n    // verification budget: DSpark schedules; others verify the full fixed block\n    var budget = (draft===&quot;dspark&quot;) ? schedule(surv, load) : g;\n\n    // simulate one accept/reject realization deterministically by survival\n    var tau=1; // anchor/bonus token always counts\n    for(var j=0;j&lt;budget;j++){ tau+=surv[j]; }\n\n    // first &quot;rejection&quot; position for the visual (first place survival dips below .5 within budget, else after budget)\n    var rejAt=-1;\n    for(var j=0;j&lt;budget;j++){ if(cond_[j]&lt;0.55){ rejAt=j; break; } }\n\n    // ---- draw tokens ----\n    var track=document.getElementById(&quot;track&quot;); track.innerHTML=&quot;&quot;;\n    function cell(lab, role, cls, conf, badge){\n      var d=document.createElement(&quot;div&quot;); d.className=&quot;tok &quot;+cls;\n      var pct=conf==null?0:Math.round(conf*100);\n      d.innerHTML='&lt;div class=&quot;role&quot;&gt;'+role+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;lab&quot;&gt;'+lab+'&lt;/div&gt;'+\n        (conf==null?'&lt;div class=&quot;cbar-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cnum&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;':\n        '&lt;div class=&quot;cbar-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cbar&quot; style=&quot;width:'+pct+'%&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cnum&quot;&gt;'+conf.toFixed(2)+'&lt;/div&gt;')+\n        (badge?'&lt;div class=&quot;badge '+badge+'&quot;&gt;'+(badge===&quot;ok&quot;?&quot;&amp;#10003;&quot;:&quot;&amp;#10007;&quot;)+'&lt;/div&gt;':'');\n      track.appendChild(d);\n    }\n    cell(&quot;D&quot;,&quot;anchor&quot;,&quot;anchor&quot;,null,null);\n    for(var k=0;k&lt;g;k++){\n      var lab=TOKENS[k]||(&quot;t&quot;+(k+1));\n      if(k&gt;=budget){ cell(lab,&quot;drop&quot;,&quot;dropped&quot;,cond_[k],null); continue; }\n      var accepted = (rejAt===-1) || (k&lt;rejAt);\n      if(accepted) cell(lab+ (k===budget-1 &amp;&amp; rejAt===-1?&quot;&quot;:&quot;&quot;),&quot;keep&quot;,&quot;accepted&quot;,cond_[k],&quot;ok&quot;);\n      else if(k===rejAt) cell(lab,&quot;keep&quot;,&quot;rejected&quot;,cond_[k],&quot;no&quot;);\n      else cell(lab,&quot;discard&quot;,&quot;dropped&quot;,cond_[k],null);\n    }\n    // corrected bonus token appended by the target on a rejection\n    if(rejAt!==-1){ cell((TOKENS[rejAt]||&quot;t&quot;)+&quot;*&quot;,&quot;fix&quot;,&quot;bonus&quot;,null,null); }\n\n    // scheduler cut marker\n    var cut=document.getElementById(&quot;cut&quot;);\n    if(draft===&quot;dspark&quot; &amp;&amp; budget&lt;g){ cut.style.display=&quot;flex&quot;;\n      document.getElementById(&quot;cut-txt&quot;).textContent=&quot;dropped &quot;+(g-budget)+&quot; low-confidence token&quot;+((g-budget)&gt;1?&quot;s&quot;:&quot;&quot;); }\n    else cut.style.display=&quot;none&quot;;\n\n    // ---- stats ----\n    document.getElementById(&quot;s-tau&quot;).textContent=tau.toFixed(2);\n    document.getElementById(&quot;s-budget&quot;).textContent=budget+1; // +1 anchor verified\n    document.getElementById(&quot;s-speed&quot;).textContent=tau.toFixed(1)+&quot;\\u00d7&quot;;\n    var saved=g-budget; document.getElementById(&quot;s-waste&quot;).textContent=(draft===&quot;dspark&quot;?saved:0);\n\n    // ---- comparison bars (paper Table 1) ----\n    var T=TABLE[domain], max=6.2;\n    function bar(id,val,cls){ var el=document.getElementById(id);\n      el.style.width=Math.round(val/max*100)+&quot;%&quot;; el.textContent=val.toFixed(2); }\n    bar(&quot;b-e3&quot;,T.eagle3,&quot;e3&quot;); bar(&quot;b-df&quot;,T.dflash,&quot;df&quot;); bar(&quot;b-ds&quot;,T.dspark,&quot;ds&quot;);\n\n    // ---- note ----\n    var note=document.getElementById(&quot;stage-note&quot;);\n    if(draft===&quot;dspark&quot;) note.textContent=&quot;DSpark drafts the block in parallel, then the load-aware scheduler keeps a confident prefix before the target verifies it.&quot;;\n    else if(draft===&quot;dflash&quot;) note.textContent=&quot;DFlash drafts the whole block in parallel and verifies all of it; acceptance decays along the suffix.&quot;;\n    else note.textContent=&quot;Eagle3 drafts sequentially with strong dependencies, but pays latency that grows with block size.&quot;;\n\n    postHeight();\n  }\n\n  // wire controls\n  function bindSeg(id, key, cast){\n    document.querySelectorAll(&quot;#&quot;+id+&quot; button&quot;).forEach(function(b){\n      b.addEventListener(&quot;click&quot;,function(){\n        document.querySelectorAll(&quot;#&quot;+id+&quot; button&quot;).forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove(&quot;on&quot;);});\n        b.classList.add(&quot;on&quot;); state[key]=cast?cast(b.dataset.v):b.dataset.v; render();\n      });\n    });\n  }\n  bindSeg(&quot;seg-draft&quot;,&quot;draft&quot;); bindSeg(&quot;seg-domain&quot;,&quot;domain&quot;);\n  document.getElementById(&quot;sl-gamma&quot;).addEventListener(&quot;input&quot;,function(e){\n    state.gamma=+e.target.value; document.getElementById(&quot;v-gamma&quot;).textContent=e.target.value; render();});\n  document.getElementById(&quot;sl-load&quot;).addEventListener(&quot;input&quot;,function(e){\n    state.load=+e.target.value; document.getElementById(&quot;v-load&quot;).textContent=e.target.value+&quot;%&quot;; render();});\n\n  // auto-resize for WordPress iframe embedding (measure our own component height)\n  function postHeight(){\n    try{ var h=document.getElementById(&quot;dspark-sim&quot;).offsetHeight+40;\n      if(window.parent){ window.parent.postMessage({type:&quot;dspark-resize&quot;,height:h},&quot;*&quot;); } }catch(e){}\n  }\n  window.addEventListener(&quot;load&quot;,postHeight);\n  window.addEventListener(&quot;resize&quot;,postHeight);\n\n  render();\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n\"></iframe>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSpec/blob/main/DSpark_paper.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Paper</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSpec\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">GitHub</a>&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-DSpark\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Model weight on HF</a></strong>.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.aidevsignals.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHub Repo OR Hugging Face Page OR Product Release OR Webinar etc.?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://forms.gle/wbash1wF6efRj8G58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark>Connect with us</mark></a></strong></p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.2.9 -->\n  <!-- https://www.molongui.com/wordpress-plugin-post-authors -->\n  <!-- CONTENT END 2 -->\n  <div class=\"td-a-rec td-a-rec-id-content_bottom  tdi_77 td_block_template_1\">\n   <div id=\"bsad-700x300\">\n    <div class=\"bs-stage\">\n     <div class=\"bs-scale\">\n      <a class=\"bs-ad\" href=\"https://pxllnk.co/cuv4rk8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"BigSet on GitHub — describe your ideal dataset in plain English, and BigSet builds it\"> \n       <div class=\"wrap\">\n        <div class=\"left\">\n         <div class=\"kicker\">\n          <span class=\"brand\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>tinyfish.ai</span><span class=\"pill\">Open Source</span>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"name\">\n          Big<b>Set</b>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"tag\">Describe your ideal dataset in plain English, and BigSet builds it.</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"right\">\n         <div class=\"cta\">\n          <span>Explore on GitHub</span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </div> \n      </a>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>","edited":null,"updateTime":"2026-06-28T21:17:14.242+00:00"}}}